# debug.cmd is a hand-run batch launcher. Keep CRLF on every checkout/platform (and every release built from a
# fresh checkout) so the repo copy always matches the shipped asset and always runs.
debug.cmd text eol=crlf

# blueStackRoot.cmd is a ~21 MB polyglot: a small CRLF batch header followed by LF-delimited base64/gzip
# payload blocks (a Magisk APK, a setuid su, the debugfs bundle). It must check out BYTE-FOR-BYTE identical
# to the shipped release asset on every platform/git config -- any EOL normalization would rewrite the
# payload lines, shift byte offsets, and can leave the embedded blocks undecodable. Mark it binary (no
# autocrlf, no eol conversion, no diff) so a clone can never corrupt the payload. See issue #24.
blueStackRoot.cmd -text -diff

# Canonical sources and tests must rebuild identically under any core.autocrlf setting.
*.ps1 text eol=lf
